From: kyoto44 (mt76 issue #1043)
Subject: mt7996: always fill TXD for all frame types to prevent TX rate collapse

All MT799x chips (MT7996, MT7992, MT7990) suffer catastrophic WiFi download
speed loss when routing IPv4 through NAT. The driver conditionally fills the
TX descriptor only for non-802.3 frames or tracked packets. Regular NATed
WiFi traffic is 802.3 without tracking -- both conditions are false, leaving
TXD zeroed. Firmware falls back to lowest MCS rate.

Fix: always call mt7996_mac_write_txwi() and always set MT_CT_INFO_APPLY_TXD.

Tested on GL-MT3600BE (MT7990/Filogic 850): download went from ~70 Mbps
(collapsing to 6 Mbps TX rate) to 1.10 Gbps on EHT160.

Ref: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1043

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1093,10 +1093,9 @@

 	pid = mt76_tx_status_skb_add(mdev, wcid, tx_info->skb);
 	memset(txwi_ptr, 0, MT_TXD_SIZE);
-	/* Transmit non qos data by 802.11 header and need to fill txd by host*/
-	if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST)
-		mt7996_mac_write_txwi(dev, txwi_ptr, tx_info->skb, wcid, key,
-				      pid, qid, 0);
+	/* Always fill txwi for firmware to avoid incorrect header processing */
+	mt7996_mac_write_txwi(dev, txwi_ptr, tx_info->skb, wcid, key,
+			      pid, qid, 0);

 	/* MT7996 and MT7992 require driver to provide the MAC TXP for AddBA
 	 * req
@@ -1145,9 +1144,8 @@
 		txp->fw.nbuf = nbuf;

 		txp->fw.flags = cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_FROM_HOST);
-
-		if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST)
-			txp->fw.flags |= cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_APPLY_TXD);
+		/* Always apply TXD to ensure correct firmware processing */
+		txp->fw.flags |= cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_APPLY_TXD);

 		if (!key)
 			txp->fw.flags |= cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_NONE_CIPHER_FRAME);
